{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Within the pomegranates.</b> The reason it repeated this expression is to say that the bells should be aligned opposite the pomegranates — that the bell should not be pulled downward or upward, but the body of the bell should be in front of the pomegranate, standing in a row, neither above nor below. And this matter is not logically entailed by its saying the first time ״the bells within the pomegranates,״ for that came only to preclude the possibility that the pomegranates would be within the bells. On that understanding, the row would begin with a bell and a pomegranate in front of it; accordingly the pomegranates would be within the bells — for the robe was not joined together at the bottom all around, such that these would always be within those as long as they are equal in number; rather, it was divided into two. And therefore you will find that the baraita did not make the number of pomegranates equal to the bells, for they are more numerous than them (Zevaḥim 88b)."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:13.766139172Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}